\/\/blog.kraken.com\/#\/schema\/person\/87e55a5e8ea020a6e620192589a05abf","name":"KrakenFX","image":{"@type":"ImageObject","inLanguage":"en-US","@id":"https:\/\/secure.gravatar.com\/avatar\/376cf5127aff2ae0a43942a0566f9d379956601670650244112b4fdb4b8c31e3?s=96&d=identicon&r=g","url":"https:\/\/secure.gravatar.com\/avatar\/376cf5127aff2ae0a43942a0566f9d379956601670650244112b4fdb4b8c31e3?s=96&d=identicon&r=g","contentUrl":"https:\/\/secure.gravatar.com\/avatar\/376cf5127aff2ae0a43942a0566f9d379956601670650244112b4fdb4b8c31e3?s=96&d=identicon&r=g","caption":"KrakenFX"},"url":"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/author\/alex-hatch"}]}},"jetpack_likes_enabled":false,"jetpack_sharing_enabled":true,"jetpack_shortlink":"https:\/\/wp.me\/peDd1v-7sS","jetpack_featured_media_url":"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/blog.kraken.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/06\/Stablr-Blog-Header.png?fit=3070%2C1400&ssl=1","_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/28698","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/230089386"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=28698"}],"version-history":[{"count":12,"href":"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/28698\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":28711,"href":"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/28698\/revisions\/28711"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/28700"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=28698"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/categories?post=28698"},{"taxonomy":"post_tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/tags?post=28698"},{"taxonomy":"language","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/language?post=28698"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}},{"id":28712,"date":"2025-06-03T08:30:32","date_gmt":"2025-06-03T12:30:32","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/?p=28712"},"modified":"2025-06-03T09:28:21","modified_gmt":"2025-06-03T13:28:21","slug":"soc-2-type-2","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/product\/security\/soc-2-type-2","title":{"rendered":"Kraken completes SOC 2 Type 2 compliance report, underscoring commitment to institutional security"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Building and maintaining a high bar for security and compliance is fundamental to how we serve our clients\u2019 needs. Today, we\u2019re pleased to announce that Kraken\u2019s institutional-grade qualified custody offering has successfully completed the SOC 2 Type 2 compliance examination \u2014 a significant milestone that further reinforces our longstanding commitment to protecting our institutional client\u2019s assets and data.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-what-soc-2-type-2-is-and-why-it-matters\"><strong>What SOC 2 Type 2 is and why it matters<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">SOC 2 (System and Organization Controls 2) is an internationally recognized framework developed by the American Institute of CPAs (AICPA) for managing customer data based on five &#8220;trust service principles&#8221;: security, availability, processing integrity, confidentiality and privacy.\u00a0<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Successfully completing the SOC 2 Type 2 examination, building on Kraken\u2019s prior <a href=\"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/news\/kraken-completes-soc-2-type-i-for-custody-and-funding-services\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">SOC 2 Type 1 report<\/a>, demonstrates not only the rigorous design of our security controls, but also their consistent execution and effectiveness over time. This independent, third-party validation builds on our existing security foundations and reflects an ongoing commitment to strengthening internal processes and technical infrastructure. These have been stress-tested to meet the highest industry standards for system reliability and the protection of sensitive data.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">&#8220;Completing the SOC 2 Type 2 examination is an important milestone, but it\u2019s just one element of our comprehensive, security-first company culture and operational strategy,&#8221; said Nick Percoco, Kraken Chief Security Officer. &#8220;We view security as a continuous, holistic commitment, one that extends beyond any single audit, reporting requirement, or certification. As Kraken continues to scale and the threat landscape evolves, we remain laser-focused on strengthening our internal controls and investing in exceptional talent to uphold our commitment to protecting our client\u2019s data and their assets.&#8221;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-what-this-means-for-our-clients\"><strong>What this means for our clients:<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Enhanced asset protection<\/strong>: SOC 2 Type 2 compliance validates that assets in Kraken\u2019s Institutional Custody platform are safeguarded by robust, industry-leading security protocols, continuously monitored and enhanced to counter evolving cybersecurity threats.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Trust through transparency<\/strong>: With this recognition, clients can have greater confidence in Kraken\u2019s operational integrity. It reaffirms how our security controls are not only well-designed, but have been reliably executed over an extended period.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Commitment to excellence:<\/strong> This achievement reflects Kraken\u2019s ongoing investment in best-in-class security practices and infrastructure, reinforcing our mission to deliver a truly security-first offering that promotes broader adoption of digital assets globally.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-a-step-forward-with-more-to-come\"><strong>A step forward, with more to come<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">SOC 2 Type 2 compliance is a significant milestone, but it&#8217;s just one part of our larger security-first philosophy at Kraken. We&#8217;re committed to continuously enhancing our infrastructure, protocols, personnel, and holistic operation to ensure we\u2019re serving our client\u2019s needs both now, and long term.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"width: 100%; height: auto; text-align: center;\"><a class=\"btn btn-primary\" style=\"display: inline-block; padding: 12px 32px; font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold; text-align: center; text-decoration: none; transition: opacity 0.2s linear 0s; line-height: 24px; border-radius: 90px; color: #FFFFFF; background-color: #5D45DC; border: 1px solid #5D45DC;\" href=\"https:\/\/www.kraken.com\/institutions\/custody\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Learn more about Kraken Institutional Custody<\/a><\/div>\n<div>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Building and maintaining a high bar for security and compliance is fundamental to how we serve our clients\u2019 needs. Today, we\u2019re pleased to announce that Kraken\u2019s institutional-grade qualified custody offering has successfully completed the SOC 2 Type 2 compliance examination \u2014 a significant milestone that further reinforces our longstanding commitment to protecting our institutional client\u2019s [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":230089386,"featured_media":28271,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_jetpack_newsletter_access":"","_jetpack_dont_email_post_to_subs":false,"_jetpack_newsletter_tier_id":0,"_jetpack_memberships_contains_paywalled_content":false,"_wpcom_ai_launchpad_first_post":false,"_jetpack_feature_clip_id":0,"_jetpack_memberships_contains_paid_content":false,"footnotes":"","jetpack_post_was_ever_published":false},"categories":[1480],"tags":[1373,1403,1409],"language":[],"class_list":["post-28712","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-security","tag-featured","tag-kraken","tag-security"],"yoast_head":"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO Premium plugin v23.2 (Yoast SEO v28.5) - https:\/\/yoast.com\/product\/yoast-seo-premium-wordpress\/ -->\n<title>Kraken completes SOC 2 Type 2 compliance report, underscoring commitment to institutional security - Kraken Blog<\/title>\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\" \/>\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/product\/security\/soc-2-type-2\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Kraken completes SOC 2 Type 2 compliance report, underscoring commitment to institutional security\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Building and maintaining a high bar for security and compliance is fundamental to how we serve our clients\u2019 needs. Today, we\u2019re pleased to announce that Kraken\u2019s institutional-grade qualified custody offering has successfully completed the SOC 2 Type 2 compliance examination \u2014 a significant milestone that further reinforces our longstanding commitment to protecting our institutional client\u2019s [&hellip;]\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/product\/security\/soc-2-type-2\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"Kraken Blog\" \/>\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2025-06-03T12:30:32+00:00\" \/>\n<meta property=\"article:modified_time\" content=\"2025-06-03T13:28:21+00:00\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/05\/3070x1400.png\" \/>\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"3070\" \/>\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"1400\" \/>\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:type\" content=\"image\/png\" \/>\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"KrakenFX\" \/>\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" \/>\n<meta name=\"twitter:label1\" content=\"Written by\" \/>\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:data1\" content=\"KrakenFX\" \/>\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:label2\" content=\"Est. reading time\" \/>\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:data2\" content=\"3 minutes\" \/>\n<script type=\"application\/ld+json\" class=\"yoast-schema-graph\">{\"@context\":\"https:\\\/\\\/schema.org\",\"@graph\":[{\"@type\":\"Article\",\"@id\":\"https:\\\/\\\/blog.kraken.com\\\/product\\\/security\\\/soc-2-type-2#article\",\"isPartOf\":{\"@id\":\"https:\\\/\\\/blog.kraken.com\\\/product\\\/security\\\/soc-2-type-2\"},\"author\":{\"name\":\"KrakenFX\",\"@id\":\"https:\\\/\\\/blog.kraken.com\\\/#\\\/schema\\\/person\\\/87e55a5e8ea020a6e620192589a05abf\"},\"headline\":\"Kraken completes SOC 2 Type 2 compliance report, underscoring commitment to institutional security\",\"datePublished\":\"2025-06-03T12:30:32+00:00\",\"dateModified\":\"2025-06-03T13:28:21+00:00\",\"mainEntityOfPage\":{\"@id\":\"https:\\\/\\\/blog.kraken.com\\\/product\\\/security\\\/soc-2-type-2\"},\"wordCount\":440,\"commentCount\":0,\"publisher\":{\"@id\":\"https:\\\/\\\/blog.kraken.com\\\/#organization\"},\"image\":{\"@id\":\"https:\\\/\\\/blog.kraken.com\\\/product\\\/security\\\/soc-2-type-2#primaryimage\"},\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https:\\\/\\\/i0.wp.com\\\/blog.kraken.com\\\/wp-content\\\/uploads\\\/2025\\\/05\\\/3070x1400.png?fit=3070%2C1400&ssl=1\",\"keywords\":[\"featured\",\"Kraken\",\"security\"],\"articleSection\":[\"Security\"],\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\",\"po